{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Complete A2 by removing the legacy field, so `bindings.json` carries no rotation bookkeeping at\nall. This is the irreversible half of A2. session_log **1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** (measured facts; do not re-derive).\n\n## Compatibility and evidence gate (no fixed delay)\n- A2-1 is merged to `main`.\n- A completed `reconcile-bridge.yml` run has a `github.sha` that is a descendant of the A2-1\n  merge commit (`git merge-base --is-ancestor`). The workflow installs from that checked-out tree,\n  so this directly proves the ephemeral writer executed the sidecar-capable build.\n- Before closure, explicitly refresh the host probe binary from a descendant of the A2-1 merge,\n  record its executable path and version/source, and prove no older reconcile/probe process remains.\n  Do not substitute elapsed time for these observations.\n\nThe writer set is the GHA reconciler and local probe runs. The canary runs only `bridge-fsck` plus\nticket CLI operations; the AWS review bot never writes `bindings.json`. Mixed-version safety is\nretained in code: a legacy writer may temporarily reintroduce an inline stamp, but the next new\nwriter reads `max(sidecar, legacy)`, persists that maximum to the sidecar, and scrubs the inline\nfield. Therefore an overlooked old process causes bounded churn and self-heals instead of losing\nrotation progress.\n\n## Approach\nStop writing `last_get_pass` in `set_last_get` and strip it from entries during save migration,\nbut retain the `max(new, legacy)` read compatibility seam. When a legacy inline value wins, persist\nthat maximum to `get_rotation.json` before removing the inline field. The read-only fallback has no\ncommitted-size cost and preserves downgrade/mixed-writer recovery.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] `last_get_pass` is absent from every entry in `bindings.json` after one\n      new-writer pass, and rotation order is preserved from `get_rotation.json` alone. Tier:\n      **integration** in a real temporary git repository.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Anti-starvation still holds: every bound-but-absent key is serviced within\n      `ceil(N/K)` passes with only the new file present. Tier: **unit** on the rotation selector.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] An old-writer/new-writer sequence that reintroduces a later inline stamp\n      migrates that maximum into `get_rotation.json`, removes the inline field, and preserves the\n      same subsequent rotation order as an all-new sequence. Tier: **integration**.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Gate evidence is recorded on this ticket: A2-1 merge SHA, descendant\n      `reconcile-bridge.yml` run id and successful ancestry result, host probe executable/version\n      after an explicit refresh, and confirmation that no older reconcile/probe process remains.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Marginal packed cost per changed version is at or below the A2-1\n      measurement. Tier: **repository-level measurement**.\n\n## Files\n`binding_store.py`, the rotation module, tests\n\nScope: S. Depends on A3 (sequencing A1 -> A2-1 -> A3 -> A2-2)."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785780334588083001,"uuid":"c5e9b4b3-8b0b-4bb1-9193-2af9e6e61fc2"}